<title>USA: Virginia jobless rate dips to 4.5 pct for July.</title>
<headline>Virginia jobless rate dips to 4.5 pct for July.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia's unemployment rate edged down to 4.5 percent in July from 4.8 percent in June, the Virginia Employment Commission said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The rate was unchanged from July of last year and represents 159,140 unemployed residents out of a civilian workforce of 3.56 million.</p>
<p>The city of Fairfax had the state's lowest unemployment rate, 1.5 percent, and Dickenson County had the higest, 19.2 percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
